{"sequence":46,"timestamp":"2026-05-03T00:27:22.481538727Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-2-c6573dbe","body":"Whole-file acceptance metric at frozenkrill-core/src/secret_sharing.rs:1: the bead's required net reduction is not met. `git diff --numstat feature/pedersen-secret-sharing..HEAD -- frozenkrill-core/src/secret_sharing.rs` reports 210 insertions and 378 deletions, a net reduction of 168 lines, but the prompt requires at least 180. Trim at least 12 more lines from this file without deleting test coverage before closing the bead.","classification":"fix_current_bead","dedup_key":"6f979c914cbc9f1cfe7c05adfeab1808d4d174a72f0b5caeaaeba822fd24e579","reviewer_sources":[{"backend_family":"codex","model_id":"gpt-5.5-xhigh","reviewer_id":"reviewer-1"}],"run_id":"run-20260502233654","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":47,"timestamp":"2026-05-03T00:27:22.494048121Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-2-cf111a85","body":"Drop the dead `verification_data` / `verification_data_hi` rewrite when constructing `SuccessEntry::verified_inputs` in `combine_vss_wallets` (`frozenkrill-core/src/secret_sharing.rs:811-816`).\n\nThe current code is:\n\n```rust\nlet verified_inputs: Vec<VssJsonWalletDescriptionV0> = vss_wallets\n.iter()\n.copied()\n.filter(|w| match &lo_set {\nSome(lo) => wallet_verifies_against_candidate(w, lo, hi_set.as_ref()),\nNone => false,\n})\n.map(|w| {\nlet mut w = w.clone();\nw.verification_data = lo_hex.to_string();\nw.verification_data_hi = hi_hex_opt.map(str::to_string);\nw\n})\n.collect();\n```\n\nThe `.clone()` is necessary (we need owned `VssJsonWalletDescriptionV0` values for `Vec`), but the field rewrite is unused. Every downstream consumer of these entries reads only `share_data`, `share_data_hi`, `original_wallet`, `share_index`, `created_at`, `threshold`, and `total_shares`:\n- `derive_metadata` (`secret_sharing.rs:843-918`) reads `share_data` and `original_wallet`.\n- `describe_share_group` (`secret_sharing.rs:1022-1046`) reads `share_index`, `created_at`, `threshold`, `total_shares`.\n- `complete_vsss_share_identifier` (`secret_sharing.rs:203-215`) reads `share_data` and `share_data_hi`.\n\nNothing reads `verification_data` or `verification_data_hi` after the verifier filter ran. Replacing the closure with `.map(|w| w.clone())` is functionally equivalent, drops a few lines, and avoids the slightly confusing artifact where `SuccessEntry`'s wallets carry verifier strings that are *neither* the share's own copy *nor* read anywhere — making it harder for future readers to reason about what state these clones represent.","classification":"fix_current_bead","dedup_key":"739e8bfd443169be985e450389249d01b1dad0b2f0dcadb406217cb60682a648","reviewer_sources":[{"backend_family":"claude","model_id":"claude-opus-4-7-max","reviewer_id":"reviewer-2"}],"run_id":"run-20260502233654","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":48,"timestamp":"2026-05-03T00:27:22.518243723Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-2-aa4d3f78","body":"Net line reduction in `frozenkrill-core/src/secret_sharing.rs` is 168 lines (210 insertions, 378 deletions) versus the bead's stated acceptance criterion of \"at least 180 lines\".\n\nMeasured via `git diff --stat feature/pedersen-secret-sharing..HEAD -- frozenkrill-core/src/secret_sharing.rs`. Branch tip is `253da64` (bead's plan_and_implement c1 r2 checkpoint); base tip is `36cc219`.\n\nThe two structural goals (drop the internal `Share` struct, drop the trailing verifier hex fields from `SuccessEntry`) are met. The shortfall is partly attributable to the ~80 lines of new test scaffolding added (`split_test_singlesig` helper + two new defense-in-depth tests for the conflict-denominator and lo/hi-splice cases). Those additions are valuable — the splice test in particular catches an attack class that would otherwise rely on `complete_vsss_share_identifier`'s implementation surviving future refactors — so I would not propose removing them to hit the line target.\n\nA combined fix would be: drop the dead-code verifier rewrite in the previous amendment (~3-4 lines), and tighten the surviving doc comments on `split_mnemonic`, `combine_one_half`, and `combine_wallet_candidate_to_mnemonic` (the docstrings are now somewhat stale post-collapse). Together that should close the gap.\n\nIf the bead reviewer judges the 12-line shortfall as acceptable given the new tests, classifying this as informational rather than a blocker is reasonable.","classification":"fix_current_bead","dedup_key":"190badc1d91d61342d33053a9300219b3e57e14e9f5424e2945dc0f1495130ab","reviewer_sources":[{"backend_family":"claude","model_id":"claude-opus-4-7-max","reviewer_id":"reviewer-2"}],"run_id":"run-20260502233654","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
